A reported missing passage already occurs in your output. Its presence does not
establish completeness: check the NUMBER of occurrences AND their positions
against the complete translation. Add another occurrence when the translation
repeats it; moving an existing occurrence cannot repair a missing repetition.
Keep every required container. Multiple repeated passages may occupy one
existing container; the number of source containers is not a content limit.

A missing passage is a missing OCCURRENCE, not a claim that its words never
appear anywhere. When the diagnostic reports missing text and ZERO extra text,
keep existing content and insert the missing occurrence at the reported gap;
merely relocating an existing occurrence leaves the output short again.
